Compared with ~/Projects/research/reports/weixue-monitor-ui-v1/03-final/*.png:
- same regions in the same order and proportions: verdict bar, held card above the band, 5-cell band, summary +
  24 h strip, sticky filter bar with counted segments, feed with time column / rail glyph / meta column, right rail
  (chats, problems, home by room); phone first screen matches phone.png (dot row, 2x2, summary, strip, search, segments).
- trace matches desktop-trace.png: six stats, Trace/Conversation/Raw, waterfall with first-token tick and gate,
  lifecycle fold line, legend, arguments/result, token split, ids.
- differences: lanes exist only for probes stored in health_probes (ha-mcp, Endpoint, Model API, Tunnel), not for
  Device/Agent/Bridge; the held card names no device; chat sub-lines show current/busy/state/mode instead of turn
  counts; the notice is labelled by its message reason (prefix_binding_mismatch on the live data).

Interaction run (playwright): search "garage" -> 1 item; Failed segment -> failed task + failure rows; Cancelled -> 1
folded item (x6); chat click filters to 1 and back to 14; Lifecycle toggle shows 40 lifecycle steps; #task=<id> opens
that trace (2 rows), Conversation 1 turn, Raw without device ids; #task=<id of a folded member> renders the linked task;
page text has no MAC and no token; "show all 4" unfolds (14 -> 17 items).
Live run: with the page scrolled 1,200 px a new task was inserted; the first visible item moved 0.5 px, the pill read
"1 new · jump to top", clicking it scrolled to the top with the new in-flight task first.

HTTP: GET / without token 401; with ?token= 200; CSP frame-ancestors http://192.168.8.142:8123 on every response;
/static/fonts/*.woff2 served as font/woff2.

